      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 5.97,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we created our first pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.97,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "the shorten pipe, and it's already working quite well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "But it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "if we could allow the user to specify the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 18.03,
          "en": "of characters, at which point you want to shorten the pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "or excuse me, shorten the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 23.22,
          "en": "Right now we're always using 10 characters as a limit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.22,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "This is hard coded into the pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 28.56,
          "en": "and this might not be the best pipes you can build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.56,
          "end": 29.79,
          "en": "Instead, it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.79,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "if we would receive a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 33.72,
          "en": "into the transform method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 36.213,
          "en": "D, let's say limit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 40.323,
          "en": "And this should simply be a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 44.61,
          "en": "Now limit would be what you then use here in the check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 48.33,
          "en": "So only if it's greater or if it has more characters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 50.07,
          "en": "than this limit, you want to shorten it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "And then of course, you use limit here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "in your substring method too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "Now with this little change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 58.65,
          "en": "you allow the user to pass a parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.65,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "to the pipe because now you receive a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 63.45,
          "en": "in the transform method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.45,
          "end": 66.54,
          "en": "And since you receive this second argument here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "the user may pass one parameter to the pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "You don't need to change anything else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 74.07,
          "en": "Don't need to change anything in the decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.07,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "This is all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "Now, with this, we can go to our app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 80.52,
          "en": "and if we would leave it like this, you see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.52,
          "end": 83.28,
          "en": "it's not short at all because we're not passing any limit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 83.28,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "therefore it's undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 88.53,
          "en": "Therefore, we always fail this check whether it is too long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 88.53,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "Therefore, we always return the original value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 95.25,
          "en": "But if we do pass a parameter, and remember we do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.25,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "by adding a colon and then the value, let's say five",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 101.67,
          "en": "if we do this and save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.67,
          "end": 105.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now you see we're shortening after five characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.53999999999999,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "And if you pick 15, now you see the first two names go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 112.05,
          "en": "through quite well because they are short enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.05,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "But these last two names are shortened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "And this is how you can of course, add multiple parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.81,
          "en": "You would add another parameter simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.81,
          "end": 124.05,
          "en": "by adding another argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.05,
          "end": 126.06,
          "en": "So this would be anotherArg",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.06,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "of the type you want it to be, whatever it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 133.41,
          "en": "And then with that added, you could simply add a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 136.26,
          "en": "colon and your second parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.26,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "This is how you parameterize your own pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 140.04,
          "en": "And of course, you could also chain them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.04,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "with built-in types and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 143.43,
          "en": "You can use it like a built-in pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 145.44,
          "en": "It's just your own pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.44,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "So this is awesome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 149.79,
          "en": "Let's now move on to an advanced use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.79,
          "end": 153.723,
          "en": "and to some limitations you might face when using pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
